world  not  because  he  can  discern  some  nearly  transparent  substance  lying 
within  his  own  three-dimensional  space,  but  because  his  senses  are  not  re¬ 
stricted  to  three  dimensions  and  have  access  to  broader  realms  of  material  or 
spiritual  reality. 

