unexpectedly  large  percentage  of  quasars  have  red  shifts  grouped  closely 
around  1.95  (BR1).  (The  red  shift  of  1.95  is  expressed  in  terms  of  shift  in 
wavelength;  it  comes  to  about  238,160  km  per  sec,  or  79  percent  of  the  speed 
