jyotiya  sastra.  Thcjyotifa  sastra  was  regarded  as  the  “eye  of  the  Vedas,"  and  it 
seemed  to  correspond  to  observable  reality.  Yet  its  description  of  the  earth 
seemed  totally  at  variance  wi  th  the  “big  earth”  of  500  m  illion  yojanas  described 
in  the  Fifth  Canto. 

